Stage 5c, part one, 10 Oct 2026. The replay bench of speech (spec 15.9,
the details of 5c) adds no library to the app. Two arms belong to the bench
alone and are not part of the app:

  The tied Nemotron pair (openconsult/bench/speech/tied), v1's pairing, run
  in the Nemotron environment of 5b. Its words model is not bundled;
  openconsult-bench speech-fetch fetches it at the pinned revision:
    nvidia/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b
      revision ea30d66debe3740a08b573244286791d423d6b3e, 2.37 GB
      OpenMDW-1.1 (its card: Use of the model is governed by the OpenMDW-1.1 license)
      https://huggingface.co/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b
    with nvidia/Nemotron-3-Diarization at the revision of stage 5b (above).
  The configuration defaults the arm copies as a plain dictionary come from
  NeMo Speech's example script speech_to_text_multitalker_streaming_infer.py
  at commit 1688cc3d6a9ade854f544987810c53f605dc86fc, Apache-2.0,
  https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Speech. Nothing of it is vendored.

  WhisperX with v1's line (openconsult/bench/speech/v1line): the WhisperX
  choice's own worker and models, loaded by path, with v1's line of drug
  names given to the live model only. No new component.

Stage 5c, part two, 11 Oct 2026. The UK drug list of the speech bench is
made by openconsult-bench speech-drugs from one month of the Prescription
Cost Analysis monthly data of the NHS Business Services Authority, from its
Open Data Portal (https://opendata.nhsbsa.net/dataset/prescription-cost-analysis-pca-monthly-data),
under the Open Government Licence v3.0: contains public sector information
licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0. Neither the file nor the
list is in the repo; the command fetches the file and makes the list on the
user's own computer. No library is added for it.

The NOTICE file on the main branch is the record for v1. It is the starting
point for any component that v2 carries from v1.

Nothing here is legal advice.

